===Etymology===
[[Image:Bastion (PSF).jpg|thumb|A bastion (1)]]
{{wikipedia}}
First attested in 1562. From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|bastion}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fr|bastille||fortress}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈbæstiən/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈbæstiən/|/ˈbæstʃən/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-bastion.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}, {{audio|en-us-bastion-2.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|Bastian}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a [[projecting]] part of a [[rampart]] or other [[fortification]]
# a well-[[fortified]] [[position]]; a [[stronghold]] or [[citadel]]
# {{label|en|figuratively}} a person, or thing, who strongly [[defend]]s some [[principle]]

